## =====================================================================
##  Slime Invasion - DirectX 11
##
##  Note: this file deliberately does NOT use blanket *.lib / *.dll rules.
##  assimp-vc143-mt.lib/.dll and lib/DirectXTex_*.lib are shipped
##  dependencies that must stay tracked - the project links them via
##  #pragma comment and copies the DLL in a post-build step.
##  Build output is excluded by directory instead, which is safer.
## =====================================================================

## --- Build output directories ---------------------------------------
[Xx]64/
[Xx]86/
[Ww]in32/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
ipch/

# Stray build tree left over from an older project layout
2dGame/

## --- Visual Studio IDE state ----------------------------------------
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.VC.db
*.VC.VC.opendb
*.aps
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.cachefile

## --- Compiler / linker intermediates --------------------------------
*.obj
*.o
*.pch
*.ipch
*.ilk
*.idb
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.pdb
*.exp
*.map
*.res
*.tli
*.tlh
*.tlog
*.lastbuildstate
*.unsuccessfulbuild

## --- Compiled shaders ------------------------------------------------
# Generated by FxCompile straight into resource/shader (see the
# ObjectFileOutput setting in 2dGame.vcxproj). Regenerated on every build,
# so keeping them in git only produces noise in every commit.
resource/shader/*.cso

## --- Misc -------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
